  "language_probability": 0.9,
  "text": "Hello Meena garu, I am the developmental paediatrician. Tell me what worries you about Asha. She is four years old and her sleep is very poor. She wakes up three or four times every night. How long has the night waking been going on? For about six months, since we moved house. During the day she is very restless. Is she taking any medicines now, and does she have any allergies? No medicines now. She is allergic to amoxicillin, she got a rash. On examination she is active, makes brief eye contact and her growth is normal for her age. During play she asked me for the bubbles with two words three times. My impression is a sleep onset and night waking problem, and I want to check for low iron. Plan: we will check a blood count and ferritin. Start melatonin two milligram tablet, one tablet by mouth thirty minutes before bed, for thirty days. Keep a fixed bedtime routine with no screens for one hour before bed. Please come back for follow up in four weeks with a sleep diary. Okay doctor, thank you.",
